    "result_text": "All 278 tests pass, including the new `Cp16Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation, following the existing pattern used for `membershipNumber`, `customerCode`, and `membershipTier`:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates into `OwnerDto`).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Integer namesakeCount` field with getter/setter.\n- **`AssignNamesakeCount.java`** (new OfficeFloor function) \u2014 counts existing stored owners sharing the new owner's last name. Since the new owner isn't persisted until the later `save` step, every matching stored owner is a distinct namesake, so no self-exclusion is needed.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignNamesakeCount` into the pipeline (under `transaction` governance) between `assignMembershipTier` and `save`.\n\nMapStruct maps `namesakeCount` onto the response DTO by name automatically. The test's `0` (first owner with the surname) and `1` (second) both pass.",
